I completely avoid it, by using the 

    ForEach ($item in $collection) {

    #doStuff with $item here 

    }

The syntax is immediately familiar to people from other programming languages and makes my code much easier to understand. 

Even though it's cool that this scripting language lets me jump in and do a for loop in the middle of a pipeline, that's a very specific concept that you don't see in other places, and I always try to stick to programming norms for better understandability in code reviews, etc.
